pipewire: accept a sound card that has no SOUND_INITIALIZED property

udev's own rules add SOUND_INITIALIZED once a card is ready, and this image has no udev daemon at all
(libudev-zero reads the devices straight from sysfs; nothing runs the rules), so the property is never
there and every card is dropped -- PipeWire comes up with no ALSA device, no sink and nothing to play to.
A kernel sound card that is there is ready; only skip one that says it is not.

--- a/spa/plugins/alsa/alsa-udev.c
+++ b/spa/plugins/alsa/alsa-udev.c
@@ -164,7 +164,11 @@
 	if ((str = udev_device_get_property_value(udev_device, "SOUND_CLASS")) && spa_streq(str, "modem"))
 		return SPA_ID_INVALID;
 
-	if (udev_device_get_property_value(udev_device, "SOUND_INITIALIZED") == NULL)
+	/* Banana: udev's own rules add SOUND_INITIALIZED once a card is ready to be used, and this image has no udev
+	 * daemon at all (libudev-zero reads the devices straight from sysfs; there is nothing to run the rules), so
+	 * the property is never there and every card is dropped -- PipeWire comes up with no ALSA device, no sink and
+	 * nothing to play to. A kernel sound card that is there is ready; only skip one that says it is not. */
+	if ((str = udev_device_get_property_value(udev_device, "SOUND_INITIALIZED")) && spa_streq(str, "0"))
 		return SPA_ID_INVALID;
 
 	if ((str = udev_device_get_property_value(udev_device, "DEVPATH")) == NULL)
